# Dreams and faith (doc 62, phase 7): rules and chains. One asks after the other's hopes, or tells their own, or a
# dream, or an omen, or asks about chapel; the other answers as they are (their drive, wealth, stage, job, quarter,
# piety, where they're from), and the first answers that in kind (warmth, humour, piety, wealth). Concepts:
# dreams.answer (what I want), dreams.reply (to someone's hope or dream), dreams.progress (any nearer it?),
# faith.answer (asked about chapel, prayer, belief), faith.reply (to an answer, an omen, a belief, a sermon). Prefix e4_.
#
# Memory, read by the next beat (2m): e4d = the kind of hope or dream just told, so dreams.reply answers that kind
# (small, big, away, content, up, rich, pup, last, love, us, family, craft, secret, jest, faith, night, nightmare, omen,
# windfall, rest, fest, slow); e4q=belief when the question was what they believe rather than whether they go; e4k = the
# kind of faith answer or remark (keen, lax, doubt, sly, work, omen, sermon, moved, folk, rich, rite, pup, old, priest), for
# faith.reply. Hard news hands to keeping.sorry / keeping.glad with k=want|grief|good (rules/keeping.talk).
# Scoring: a grown wolf's answer scores 2 (two criteria, or one and priority 1), so every answer that fits a speaker
# shares one tier; pups, adolescents, the destitute, beggars, mourners and priests answer with a priority, as
# themselves. Replies are keyed (priority 1) and their trait variants add one fact.

## ================================================================ DREAMS: asking

rule e4_rd_ask
when concept=talk.dreams
cooldown 1d
say If you could have anything at all, what would it be? | What do you want out of life, #address#? Truly. | Ever think about what's next? For you, I mean. | Got any plans? Big ones? | What would you wish for, if wishing worked?
then other: dreams.answer
remember pair: e4_hopes 14d
remember other: e4_hoped 14d

rule e4_rd_ask_close
when concept=talk.dreams pair.band=friends|family|spouses
cooldown 2d
say Tell me something you want, #pet#. Something just for you. | What's your dream these days? You never say. | If it all went right, where would you be in ten years?
then other: dreams.answer
remember pair: e4_hopes 14d
remember other: e4_hoped 14d

rule e4_rd_ask_pup
when concept=talk.dreams other.stage=young self.stage=adult|old
cooldown 1d
say What'll you be when you're grown, #address#? | Do you know what you want to be yet? | When you're big, what will you do? | What's the best thing you could be, when you're grown?
then other: dreams.answer
remember pair: e4_hopes 14d
remember other: e4_hoped 14d

rule e4_rd_ask_old
when concept=talk.dreams other.stage=old self.stage!=old
cooldown 2d
say Anything you've still a mind to do? | If you could have one more thing, what would it be? | Is there anything you always meant to do and never did?
then other: dreams.answer
remember pair: e4_hopes 14d
remember other: e4_hoped 14d

rule e4_rd_ask_spouse
when concept=talk.dreams pair.band=spouses
cooldown 3d
say When we're old and grey, what'll we do, #dear#? | If we'd the coin, where would you want us to live? | Tell me what you want for us. Not the roof. Us.
then other: dreams.answer
remember pair: e4_hopes 14d
remember other: e4_hoped 14d

rule e4_rd_ask_apprentice
when concept=talk.dreams pair.band=apprentice other.apprentice=yes
cooldown 3d
say What sort of master will you be, when it's your turn? | Where do you see yourself, when your time's done here? | You've got a dream in that head. Out with it.
then other: dreams.answer
remember pair: e4_hopes 14d
remember other: e4_hoped 14d

rule e4_rd_progress
when concept=talk.dreams pair.mem.e4_hopes other.mem.e4_hoped
cooldown 3d
say Any nearer that dream of yours? | How's the big plan coming? | Still set on what you told me? | That thing you wanted. Any closer?
then other: dreams.progress

## ================================================================ DREAMS: telling one's own

rule e4_rd_tell_night
when concept=talk.dreams
cooldown 1d
say Had the strangest dream last night. I was a fish, and I was late. | Dreamt I was at my own wedding and couldn't find my boots. | I dreamt the moon came down and sat on the well. Nobody minded. | Dreamt I could talk to hens. Dreadful company. | Dreamt the whole town was made of bread, and it was raining.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=night 2m

rule e4_rd_tell_bad
when concept=talk.dreams here.time=dawn|day
cooldown 2d
say Bad dream. I'm still shaking it off. | Didn't sleep well. Dreamt I was lost in the fog and couldn't find my door. | Dreamt the floor gave way. Woke on the boards. | Dreamt I was calling and calling, and nobody turned round.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=nightmare 2m

rule e4_rd_tell_omen
when concept=talk.dreams self.piety=devout
cooldown 2d
say I dreamt of a white bird on the chapel roof. That means something. | Three nights, the same dream. A lamp in a window. It's a sign. | I dream true, you know. My mother did too. | I dreamt of the chapel bell ringing by itself. Three nights now.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=omen 2m

rule e4_rd_tell_windfall
when concept=talk.dreams self.wealth=poor|comfortable
cooldown 2d
say If I came into money, I'd buy every pie on the stall. Then the stall. | Say a purse fell out of the sky. I've already spent it in my head. Twice. | If my old aunt left me a fortune, I'd not tell a soul. Except you. Maybe.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=windfall 2m

rule e4_rd_tell_ambitious
when concept=talk.dreams self.drive=ambitious self.stage=adult|old
cooldown 2d
say I've a plan, and it's a good one, and I'm not telling. Yet. | Two years. Two years and I'll be the one giving the orders. | Mark me: one day they'll know my name in every town on the roads. | I'm not stopping where I am. Not for anyone.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=big 2m

rule e4_rd_tell_restless
when concept=talk.dreams self.drive=restless self.stage=adult|old
cooldown 2d
say I can't stay here much longer. I'll go mad. | Every time a cart goes by I want to be on it. | I keep looking at the road like it owes me something. | One morning I'll walk out of the gate and just keep going.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=away 2m

rule e4_rd_tell_content
when concept=talk.dreams self.drive=content self.stage=adult|old
cooldown 2d
say Know what I want? Nothing. I've got it. | Folk keep asking about my plans. My plan is supper. | I sat in the sun this morning and thought, this'll do. | Some want the world. I want this step, of an evening.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=content 2m

rule e4_rd_tell_sump
when concept=talk.dreams self.quarter=sump self.stage!=young
cooldown 2d
say One day I'll have a room on the hill. Windows. Air. | No pup of mine grows up down here. I swear it. | Getting out of the Sump. That's the only dream down here.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=up 2m

rule e4_rd_tell_poor
when concept=talk.dreams self.wealth=poor|destitute self.stage!=young
cooldown 2d
say If I were rich, I'd have a fire all night. Every night. | One day I'll buy bread without counting the pennies first. | A whole pie. To myself. That's my dream, these days.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e4_rd_tell_rich
when concept=talk.dreams self.wealth=rich self.stage=adult|old
cooldown 3d
say I'm thinking of buying an orchard. Not to work. To walk in. | Do you know, I'd like to do something useful with it all. Just once. | Money's a dull dream once you've got it. I want something else.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=rich 2m

rule e4_rd_tell_young
when concept=talk.dreams self.stage=young
cooldown 1d
say When I'm big I'm going to be a baker and eat all the mistakes. | I'm going to have a boat and a hat and a sword. | I'm going to be a hero. A real one. With a song. | When I'm grown I'll have the biggest ears in town. You'll see.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=pup 2m

rule e4_rd_tell_adolescent
when concept=talk.dreams self.stage=adolescent
cooldown 2d
say Soon as I'm old enough, I'm off. Over the hills. Anywhere. | I'm going to be something nobody here's even heard of. | I'll learn a trade this town hasn't got. Then they'll see.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=away 2m

rule e4_rd_tell_old
when concept=talk.dreams self.stage=old
cooldown 2d
say I've decided to live to a hundred. Just to annoy my nephew. | One more good summer. That's all I'm asking for. | I'd like to dance once more. Properly. Before the knees go altogether.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=last 2m

rule e4_rd_tell_unwed
when concept=talk.dreams self.married=no self.stage=adult
cooldown 3d
say I'd like to be married, #someday#. A full house, a loud one. | I keep thinking I should find someone. Then I don't. | I'd like somebody to walk out with. Somebody kind. Is that so daft?
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=love 2m

rule e4_rd_tell_parent
when concept=talk.dreams self.parent=yes self.child self.age<=45
cooldown 3d
say #self.child# wants to go to sea. I've said no. They've not listened. | All I want is for #self.child# to have it better than I did. | #self.child# says they'll buy me a house one day. I'm holding them to it.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=family 2m

rule e4_rd_tell_house
when concept=talk.dreams self.house self.wealth!=rich self.stage=adult
cooldown 3d
say Our steward's getting on. Somebody'll step up. Why not me? | I've been noticed up at the House. The steward said my name. Twice. | Give it ten years and I'll have a desk at the House. Mark me.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=big 2m

rule e4_rd_tell_apprentice
when concept=talk.dreams self.apprentice=yes pair.band!=apprentice
cooldown 2d
say When I've my own mark, I'll put it on everything. Even spoons. | Two more years and I'm my own master. | I'm going to be better than my master. Don't tell them.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=craft 2m

rule e4_rd_tell_widowed
when concept=talk.dreams self.widowed=yes
cooldown 3d
say I had my dream. Twenty years of it. I don't need another. | I dream of them most nights, my old love. I don't mind it. | We always meant to go south, the two of us. I might go yet. For both of us.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=grief 2m

rule e4_rd_tell_owes
when concept=talk.dreams self.owes=yes
cooldown 3d
say My dream? To owe nobody a penny. Just once. | One day I'll walk down the street and not cross over to avoid anyone. | If I could clear my debts I'd sleep a week.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e4_rd_tell_failing
when concept=talk.dreams self.business=failing
cooldown 3d
say I dreamed of this place for ten years. Now look at it. | I just want the doors open past the month. That's my whole dream now. | Funny. You get the dream, and then you have to keep it.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e4_rd_tell_thriving
when concept=talk.dreams self.business=thriving
cooldown 3d
say Another year like this and I'll take on more paws. | I've dreamed of this since I was a pup. And here it is. | Next I want a sign. Painted. Gold letters.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=good 2m

rule e4_rd_tell_festival
when concept=talk.dreams world.festival=soon here.festival
cooldown 2d
say I'm going to win something at #here.festival#. Don't know what yet. | I've a plan for #here.festival#. It involves dancing. | This #here.festival# I'm going to tell someone something. Brave, me.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=fest 2m

rule e4_rd_tell_restday
when concept=talk.dreams here.day=work|market self.shift=after
cooldown 2d
say Restday, I'm doing nothing. I've planned it all out. | I'm going to sleep through Restday. Chapel can come to me. | Restday I'm going up the hill with bread and cheese and nobody.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=rest 2m

rule e4_rd_tell_north
when concept=talk.dreams self.from=frosthollow
cooldown 3d
say I'd like one winter where my ears don't hurt. Just one. | Someone told me in the south the snow never comes. Can you imagine? | I'll go down the valley one day and not come back up. Maybe.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=small 2m

rule e4_rd_tell_fen
when concept=talk.dreams self.from=mirebridge
cooldown 3d
say Dry boots. That's a fen wolf's whole dream. Dry boots. | A house on a hill. Any hill. | One day I'll live where the floor doesn't squelch.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=small 2m

rule e4_rd_tell_south
when concept=talk.dreams self.from=southmeadow|larkfield
cooldown 3d
say I want my own orchard. Twenty trees. Every one with a name. | One good year, and I'll buy the bottom field off my neighbour. | A field by the river, black soil, no landlord.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=small 2m

rule e4_rd_tell_city
when concept=talk.dreams self.from=ridgemere here.region!=ridgemere
cooldown 3d
say I miss the Sound, you know. I'll go back one day. | Funny. I left the city to get away, and now I dream of it. | One day I'll go home and smell the salt again. Rain and all.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=away 2m

## ================================================================ DREAMS: answering (self answers what they want)

rule e4_rd_ans_small
when concept=dreams.answer wealth=poor|comfortable stage=adult|old
say Honestly? A bit of peace. A chair by a fire that's mine. | Good boots and no debts. I'm not greedy. | A roof that doesn't leak, and a lock that works. | A garden. Beans, a bench, and nobody telling me what to plant.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=small 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_own
when concept=dreams.answer business=none wealth=poor|comfortable
say My own shop. Small. My name over the door. | A cottage. Low roof, a garden, a bench by the door. | A boat. Painted. Mine. | Something with my name on it. A door, a cart, a field. Anything.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=small 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_steady
when concept=dreams.answer drive=steady stage=adult|old
say Same as now, but a bit better. A good winter. | Keep on as I am, put a bit by. Nothing fancy. | A steady year. No surprises. I hate surprises.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=small 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_content
when concept=dreams.answer drive=content stage=adult|old
say This. I've got it. A roof, a fire, folk to talk to. | Nothing much. Same again, a bit warmer. | Why? What's wrong with now?
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=content 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_restless
when concept=dreams.answer drive=restless stage=adult|old
say Out. Anywhere. The sea, the mountains, I don't mind which. | To go where the roads go. All of them. | Something different. Every day the same is killing me.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=away 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_ambitious
when concept=dreams.answer drive=ambitious stage=adult|old
say My name on everyone's lips. For good reasons, mostly. | To matter. To be the name folk say first. | To be the one folk come to. The one who decides. | More than this. Much more. I'll know it when I've got it.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=big 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_poor
when concept=dreams.answer wealth=poor stage=adult|old
say Meat on a weekday. Every weekday. | A second coat, for when the first's wet. | Bread without counting. That's all.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_destitute
when concept=dreams.answer wealth=destitute stage!=young
priority 3
say A full belly. Ask me after that. | A dry corner. Tonight, if you've got one. | Dreams cost money, #address#. I've none.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_rich
when concept=dreams.answer wealth=rich stage=adult|old
say I've most things. I'd like some time, I suppose. | A good name, after. That's what lasts. | Something money can't buy. Don't laugh.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=rich 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_sump
when concept=dreams.answer quarter=sump wealth!=rich
say Out of the Sump. Up the hill. Air. | A door that locks, and nobody on the other side of the wall. | My pups up the hill. Me too, if there's room.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=up 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_heights
when concept=dreams.answer quarter=heights wealth=rich|comfortable
say To be let alone at a party. Just once. | To walk to market without a footman. | Truthfully? To be ordinary for a week.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=rich 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_young
when concept=dreams.answer stage=young
priority 5
say A smith! With the big hammer! | A sailor, and go everywhere, and never wash. | A hero. Or a baker. Bakers get cake. | The one who rings the chapel bell. | Big. Bigger than my brother.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=pup 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_adolescent
when concept=dreams.answer stage=adolescent
priority 4
say Anything but what they want me to be. | Somewhere bigger than here. Anywhere. | I don't know. That's the worst of it. | Out. Just out. I'll work out the rest on the road.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=away 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_old
when concept=dreams.answer stage=old
priority 1
say To see the young ones settled. That's all I'm waiting on. | A long sit in the sun with nobody asking me anything. | To go in my own bed, with the window open. Not yet, mind.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=last 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_merchant
when concept=dreams.answer job=merchant business!=failing
say My name on a warehouse, in paint. | Trade with every town on the roads. | To be the one the others copy.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=big 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_farmer
when concept=dreams.answer job=farmer|herder wealth!=rich
say A good pony and a dry barn. That's farming done right. | My own ground, where the soil's black. | One harvest where nothing goes wrong. Just one.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=small 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_fisher
when concept=dreams.answer job=fisher|sailor wealth!=rich
say A net that doesn't want mending every night. | One season where the water gives more than it takes. | A boat with a dry hold and a crew that listens.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=small 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_miner
when concept=dreams.answer job=miner wealth!=rich
say To see my grandpups and not cough at them. | A house with a window facing east. Morning sun. | To hang up the lamp, and never light it again.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=up 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_guard
when concept=dreams.answer job=guard|soldier stage=adult|old
say A posting at a quiet gate in a quiet town. | To be the one who trains the new ones. | Boots that fit and a captain who listens.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=small 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_servant
when concept=dreams.answer job=servant|laborer wealth!=rich
say A day off that's mine, not half of one. | My own place. My own fire. Nobody's bell. | To sit down. A whole day, sat down.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=up 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_crafter
when concept=dreams.answer job=crafter|smith|apprentice wealth!=rich
say My own mark, on good work. | To make one thing that lasts a hundred years. | My own bench. My own door. My own tools.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=craft 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_priest
when concept=dreams.answer job=priest
priority 1
say To bury fewer young ones. | A chapel kitchen that never runs out of bread. | That folk would come when things are good, not only when they're bad.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=faith 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_beggar
when concept=dreams.answer job=beggar
priority 3
say Shoes. Then a roof. In that order. | One winter indoors. | A bowl of something hot, and nobody moving me on.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_mourning
when concept=dreams.answer mourning=kin|friend stage!=young
priority 3
say Ask me another week. I've no dreams this one. | Just for them to be back. That's all, and it's not coming. | To have said goodbye properly. That's my dream now.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=grief 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_unwed
when concept=dreams.answer married=no stage=adult
say Somebody to come home to. | A wedding in the orchard. Somebody else's first, to practise. | A spouse, a full house and a pot always on.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=love 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_parent
when concept=dreams.answer parent=yes stage=adult|old
say For my pups to have it better than me. That's all. | To see mine grown and happy. Then I'll dream for myself. | Honestly? A night's sleep.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=family 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_spouse
when concept=dreams.answer self.spouse pair.band!=spouses
say Me and #self.spouse#, old and grumpy, in the same chairs. | Somewhere sunny for #self.spouse# and me. One day. | Ask #self.spouse#. They do the dreaming for both of us.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=us 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_to_spouse
when concept=dreams.answer pair.band=spouses stage!=young
priority 2
say You and me, in the same two chairs, arguing about the draught. | A bit of garden. You'd dig, I'd sit. That's fair. | Somewhere warm, with you in it. That's the lot. | Just more of this. Fewer bills.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=us 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_to_master
when concept=dreams.answer pair.band=apprentice apprentice=yes
priority 2
say My own bench, and an apprentice who listens better than I did. | A shop of my own. Not too near yours, don't worry. | To be half as good as you. Then the other half.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=craft 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_owes
when concept=dreams.answer owes=yes stage!=young
priority 1
say To owe nobody. Not a penny. | Clear my debts and sleep for a week. | Ask me when I've paid what I owe.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_guarded
when concept=dreams.answer honesty=guarded stage=adult|old
say That's my business. | I'll tell you when I've got it. | Not saying. Then it can't be laughed at.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=secret 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_merry
when concept=dreams.answer humour=merry stage=adult|old
say A barrel that never empties and a chair that never breaks. | To be taller. Failing that, richer. | A bed big enough to lose someone in.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=jest 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_dry
when concept=dreams.answer humour=dry stage=adult|old
say Fewer questions like this one. | To win an argument with my mother. Just once. | A quiet life. Clearly I'm in the wrong town.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=jest 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_devout
when concept=dreams.answer piety=devout stage=adult|old
say Whatever the Bright One has for me. | A good death, a long way off. And a clean conscience. | To do some good before I go.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=faith 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_north
when concept=dreams.answer from=frosthollow stage=adult|old
say A south-facing house with a stove in every room. | Toes I can feel in midwinter. | A summer somewhere they've never heard of snow.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=small 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_fen
when concept=dreams.answer from=mirebridge stage=adult|old
say A house on stilts so high the fen gives up. | Boots that stay dry past breakfast. | To grow old somewhere the floor doesn't move.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=small 2m

rule e4_rd_ans_south
when concept=dreams.answer from=southmeadow|larkfield stage=adult|old
say A barn full to the rafters at harvest. Once. | To take a cart to Ridgemere and sell straight off the wharf. | A press of my own, and apples to fill it.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=small 2m

## ================================================================ DREAMS: replying (self heard the other's hope or dream)

rule e4_rd_rep_fallback
when concept=dreams.reply
say Here's hoping. | You'll get there. | Good dream, that.

# --- a pup listening to a grown-up's hope or dream
rule e4_rd_rep_young_hope
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=small|big|away|content|up|rich|love|us|family|craft|secret|jest|faith|windfall|rest|fest|slow stage=young other.stage!=young
priority 2
say Is that a good one? | When I'm big I'll want that too. Maybe. | Oh. I'd want a pony. | Can I help?

rule e4_rd_rep_young_dream
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=night|nightmare|omen stage=young
priority 2
say Was it scary? | I dream about cake. | I had one like that! Nearly.

# --- a small, homely hope (a roof, a boat, dry boots, a field)
rule e4_rd_rep_small
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=small
priority 1
say Not much to ask. You'll have it. | That's a good one. Plain and good. | Here's hoping. It's not a lot to want. | You'll get there. A bit at a time. | I'd want the same, near enough.

rule e4_rd_rep_small_warm
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=small warmth=warm
priority 1
say You deserve that and more, #pet#. | Oh, I hope you get it. I'll help, if I can. | I'll come and sit by your fire, when you've got it. If I'm asked.

rule e4_rd_rep_small_cold
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=small warmth=cold
priority 1
say Hm. Dreams are cheap. | Most want that. Few get it. | If you say so.

rule e4_rd_rep_small_dry
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=small humour=dry
priority 1
say Steady on. Don't go mad. | Wild. I'd never have guessed. | Mind you don't get above yourself.

rule e4_rd_rep_small_ambitious
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=small drive=ambitious
priority 1
say That's all? Aim higher. | Small. Think bigger, #address#. | Then start tomorrow. Nobody gets anything by wishing.

rule e4_rd_rep_small_rich
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=small wealth=rich other.wealth=poor|destitute
priority 1
say That's not so much to want. Shame on the rest of us. | If you ever need a start, come and see me. | I'd forgotten folk wanted so little.

rule e4_rd_rep_small_old
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=small stage=old other.stage!=old
priority 1
say Don't wait too long for it. It goes quick. | I wanted that at your age. I still do.

# --- a big, ambitious hope
rule e4_rd_rep_big
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=big
priority 1
say Bold. I'll say that. | We'll see. Good luck to you. | I believe it. Somebody has to. | Big talk. Mind you back it up. | Remember us when you're grand.

rule e4_rd_rep_big_content
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=big drive=content
priority 1
say Sounds like a lot of bother. | Higher the perch, colder the wind. | And when you've got it, then what?

rule e4_rd_rep_big_ambitious
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=big drive=ambitious
priority 1
say We'll see who's first. | Move over, then. | Good. I like company at the top.

rule e4_rd_rep_big_rival
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=big pair.band=rivals
priority 2
say Not before me, you won't. | We'll see about that. | Good luck. You'll need it.

rule e4_rd_rep_big_frank
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=big honesty=frank
priority 1
say You said that last year. | Then stop telling me and do it. | Less talk, more doing.

rule e4_rd_rep_big_merry
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=big humour=merry
priority 1
say Ha! Save me a seat at your table. | And me at your right paw, I hope. | I'll drink to that. I'll drink to anything, mind.

# --- going away: the road, the sea, out of here
rule e4_rd_rep_away
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=away
priority 1
say Go, then. Before you can't. | Send word when you get there. | I'd miss you. Go anyway. | Bring me back something. Anything. | Mind the roads. They're not what they were.

rule e4_rd_rep_away_restless
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=away drive=restless
priority 1
say Take me with you. | I've thought the same. More than once. | Say when. I mean it.

rule e4_rd_rep_away_content
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=away drive=content
priority 1
say Every road comes back here in the end. | The hills look the same from the other side. | I've saved myself the walk.

rule e4_rd_rep_away_old
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=away stage=old other.stage!=old
priority 1
say Do it before your knees go. | I wanted that, at your age. I never went. | Go while your legs are good.

rule e4_rd_rep_away_youth
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=away other.stage=adolescent stage=adult|old
priority 2
say Grow a bit first. The road'll keep. | Finish growing first. | Go when you're grown. I'll not stop you.

rule e4_rd_rep_away_spouse
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=away pair.band=spouses
priority 2
say And leave me here? Take me too. | You've never told me that. | Then we'll go. Together, mind.

# --- content with their lot
rule e4_rd_rep_content
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=content
priority 1
say Lucky. Truly. | Not many can say that. | Hold onto it, then. | I'd drink to that.

rule e4_rd_rep_content_ambitious
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=content drive=ambitious
priority 1
say That's it? Truly? | I'd go mad in a week. | Each to their own. Mine's bigger.

rule e4_rd_rep_content_poor
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=content wealth=poor|destitute other.wealth=comfortable|rich
priority 1
say Easy to be content with a full larder. | Must be nice. | Swap you.

rule e4_rd_rep_content_content
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=content drive=content
priority 1
say Same here. Pull up a chair. | Wise wolf. | That's the trick of it. Most never learn.

# --- out of a hard lot: the Sump, the mine, service
rule e4_rd_rep_up
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=up
priority 1
say You'll get there. I'd put money on it. | Good. Hold onto that. | That's not much to want. It's everything, but it's not much. | Then go, and don't look back.

rule e4_rd_rep_up_sump
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=up quarter=sump
priority 1
say Everyone down here says that. Few go. | Take me with you when you go. | If anyone gets out, it'll be you.

rule e4_rd_rep_up_miner
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=up job=miner
priority 1
say Same thought, every shift. | Up the cage at dusk, and I think it every time. | Daylight. Aye. I'd give a lot.

rule e4_rd_rep_up_warm
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=up warmth=warm
priority 1
say And when you do, I'll carry the first box. | You will. And I'll be glad of it. | Hold onto that. Don't let anyone take it.

rule e4_rd_rep_up_rich
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=up wealth=rich
priority 1
say I'd not thought it was so hard. I should have. | If you need a word put in somewhere, ask me. | That's not much to want. Shame on us.

# --- a rich wolf's dream
rule e4_rd_rep_rich
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=rich
priority 1
say Well. If anyone can, you can. | There's a thing to want. | I'd not know where to start. | I'll take your word for it.

rule e4_rd_rep_rich_poor
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=rich wealth=poor|destitute
priority 1
say Must be nice, dreaming that big. | Some of us dream of supper. | Lucky you.

rule e4_rd_rep_rich_rich
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=rich wealth=rich
priority 1
say We all say that. Then the season starts. | I know just what you mean. | Do it. One of us should.

rule e4_rd_rep_rich_dry
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=rich humour=dry
priority 1
say Poor you. | The burdens you carry. | I'll hold a collection.

# --- a pup's dream
rule e4_rd_rep_pup
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=pup
priority 1
say Are you, now? | You'll be the best one. | I believe it. | Practise, then. Start today.

rule e4_rd_rep_pup_pup
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=pup stage=young
priority 2
say Me too! Me too! | Can I come? | I'm going to be a better one.

rule e4_rd_rep_pup_guard
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=pup job=guard|soldier
priority 1
say Stand up straight, then. Start now. | We'll want you. Grow fast. | Practise your growl.

rule e4_rd_rep_pup_warm
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=pup warmth=warm
priority 1
say Course you will, little one. | I'll come and watch. Front row. | That's the best one I've heard all week.

# --- the old: what's left to want
rule e4_rd_rep_last
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=last
priority 1
say Not for a long while yet. | That's not much to ask. | You've earned that and more. | I'll hold you to it.

rule e4_rd_rep_last_young
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=last stage=young
priority 2
say Are you very old? | How old? Older than the well? | I'll come and see you every day.

rule e4_rd_rep_last_old
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=last stage=old
priority 1
say Same here. One more summer, and then another. | Aye. That'd do me too. | We'll creak through it together.

rule e4_rd_rep_last_warm
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=last warmth=warm
priority 1
say And I'll be there, with a cake. | You'll have that. I'll see you do. | Oh, you'll see plenty more.

# --- love: someone to come home to
rule e4_rd_rep_love
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=love
priority 1
say You'll find them. Or they'll find you. | Somebody'll be lucky. | Don't hurry it. It comes when it comes. | Look for the one who laughs at your jokes.

rule e4_rd_rep_love_married
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=love married=yes
priority 1
say Find one who'll share the blankets. | It's worth it. Most days. | Mine snores. I'd not swap.

rule e4_rd_rep_love_merry
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=love humour=merry
priority 1
say I'll dance at that wedding. Badly. | Somebody with a name? I'll find out. | Put me down for the first dance.

rule e4_rd_rep_love_old
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=love stage=old
priority 1
say Ah. I remember wanting that. Enjoy the wanting. | You'll have it. Then you'll want quiet. | Don't wait for perfect. Nobody's perfect.

# --- us: a couple's dream (told about a spouse, or to them)
rule e4_rd_rep_us
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=us
priority 1
say That's a good one. Grow old together. | Sounds like you've got it already. | You'll have it, the pair of you.

rule e4_rd_rep_us_spouse
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=us pair.band=spouses
priority 2
say Then we'll do it. Together. | You've never told me that. I like it. | Same chairs. I'll want a cushion. | I'll start saving. Don't tell me it's daft.

# --- a parent's hope for their pups
rule e4_rd_rep_family
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=family
priority 1
say They will. You'll see to it. | They're lucky to have you. | That's all any of us want.

rule e4_rd_rep_family_parent
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=family parent=yes
priority 1
say Mine too. Every night I wish it. | Same here. They'd better be grateful. | Ours'll do better. They have to.

# --- a trade: their own mark, their own bench
rule e4_rd_rep_craft
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=craft
priority 1
say You'll get there, if you keep at it. | Good. Want it. Wanting's half the work. | Mind you finish what you start, then.

rule e4_rd_rep_craft_master
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=craft master=yes
priority 1
say Keep your edges clean and you will. | Then stop talking and sharpen something. | Good. I was the same. Still am.

# --- kept close, or turned into a joke
rule e4_rd_rep_secret
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=secret
priority 1
say Fair enough. | Keep it, then. Keep it safe. | I'll not laugh. When you're ready. | Suit yourself.

rule e4_rd_rep_secret_chatty
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=secret talk=chatty
priority 1
say I'll get it out of you. I've time. | Not even a hint? Mean. | You'll tell me. Everyone does.

rule e4_rd_rep_jest
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=jest
priority 1
say Ha! Fair. | I walked into that. | I'll stop asking, then. | Daft beast.

rule e4_rd_rep_jest_merry
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=jest humour=merry
priority 1
say Ha! And me there with you, I hope. | Make room for me. I'll bring the ale. | Now that's a dream worth having.

rule e4_rd_rep_jest_short
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=jest temper=short
priority 1
say I asked you a proper question. | Suit yourself. I'll not ask again. | Funny. Very funny.

# --- a devout wish
rule e4_rd_rep_faith
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=faith
priority 1
say That's a good wish. | Better than mine. | The Bright One'd like that. | Bless you for it.

rule e4_rd_rep_faith_devout
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=faith piety=devout
priority 1
say And mine. Exactly that. | I'll pray you get it. | #blessing#. You'll do good. You do already.

rule e4_rd_rep_faith_frank
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=faith honesty=frank piety=ordinary
priority 1
say That's not a dream, that's a sermon. | Very holy. What do you actually want? | Fair. I'd want a pie, myself.

# --- last night's dreams
rule e4_rd_rep_night
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=night
priority 1
say Strange old world#tag#. | Cheese before bed again? | That's a new one. | Better than mine. I dreamt of turnips. | I'll not sleep for thinking about that.

rule e4_rd_rep_night_dry
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=night humour=dry
priority 1
say Riveting. Go on. No, don't. | Fascinating. Truly. | I'll be thinking about that all day. Sadly.

rule e4_rd_rep_night_merry
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=night humour=merry
priority 1
say Ha! I'll dream of that tonight now. Thanks. | Tell me there was more. | Ha! Was I in it?

rule e4_rd_rep_night_old
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=night stage=old
priority 1
say My mother would have had that read. | I've not dreamt anything in years. Lucky you. | I stopped dreaming at sixty. I don't miss it.

rule e4_rd_rep_nightmare
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=nightmare
priority 1
say Ugh. I hate those. | Shake it off. You're awake now. | Only a dream. It's gone now. | Have something hot. It helps.

rule e4_rd_rep_nightmare_warm
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=nightmare warmth=warm
priority 1
say You're all right now. I've got you. | Sit a while. Get warm. | Oh, #pet#. Walk with me a bit.

rule e4_rd_rep_nightmare_cold
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=nightmare warmth=cold
priority 1
say Everybody dreams. | Hm. | It'll pass by noon.

rule e4_rd_rep_omen
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=omen
priority 1
say If you say so. | Could be. | I'd not read too much into it. | Let's hope it's a good something.

rule e4_rd_rep_omen_devout
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=omen piety=devout
priority 1
say The Bright One speaks how he likes. Pray on it. | I believe you. Watch for it. | Then mind what it tells you.

rule e4_rd_rep_omen_frank
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=omen honesty=frank
priority 1
say It means you slept badly. That's all. | Dreams are dreams. | Your mother said a lot of things, I expect.

# --- a windfall, spent in the head
rule e4_rd_rep_windfall
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=windfall
priority 1
say And where am I in all this? | Mind you remember your friends. | I'd do the same. Then worse. | Spent already, and not a penny of it real.

rule e4_rd_rep_windfall_poor
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=windfall wealth=poor|destitute
priority 1
say A ham. A whole one. Then another. | Pay what I owe. Then something daft. | Dream on. I do.

rule e4_rd_rep_windfall_rich
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=windfall wealth=rich
priority 1
say It goes quicker than you'd think. | Put half by. You'll thank me. | It's never as much as you think.

# --- Restday and festival plans
rule e4_rd_rep_rest
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=rest
priority 1
say Lucky you. | Good plan. | Nobody's earned it more. | I'll believe it when I see it.

rule e4_rd_rep_rest_spouse
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=rest pair.band=spouses
priority 2
say And the gutter? It's been waiting since spring. | Not with that hen-house half built, you're not. | We'll see what the pups say.

rule e4_rd_rep_rest_devout
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=rest piety=devout
priority 1
say Chapel first. Then nothing. | Say your prayers before you do nothing. | The Bright One rested too. Fair.

rule e4_rd_rep_fest
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=fest
priority 1
say I'll be watching. | I'll hold you to that. | Brave. Good. | I'll come and see.

rule e4_rd_rep_fest_merry
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=fest humour=merry
priority 1
say I'll be right beside you. Making it worse. | Ha! Count me in. | Then I'm coming early.

# --- any nearer? not really
rule e4_rd_rep_slow
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=slow
priority 1
say Slow's still going. | Keep at it. | A penny's a penny. | It'll come.

rule e4_rd_rep_slow_dry
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=slow humour=dry
priority 1
say At that pace you'll be there by your funeral. | Steady. Don't wear yourself out. | Next year, then. Or the one after.

rule e4_rd_rep_slow_warm
when concept=dreams.reply pair.mem.e4d=slow warmth=warm
priority 1
say I'm proud of you for holding on. | Not letting go's the hard part. You're doing it. | Bit by bit. That's how it's done.

## ================================================================ DREAMS: any nearer? (self answers)

rule e4_rd_prog_plain
when concept=dreams.progress
say Not a step. But I've not let go. | Bit nearer. A penny nearer. | Ask me next year. | Still set on it. Still a long way off.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=slow 2m

rule e4_rd_prog_thriving
when concept=dreams.progress business=thriving
priority 1
say Nearer! Good season. I can nearly touch it. | It's coming. I can feel it coming. | Closer than I've ever been.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=good 2m

rule e4_rd_prog_poor
when concept=dreams.progress wealth=poor|destitute stage!=young
priority 1
say Further, if anything. | I spent the jar on the rent. | Dreams don't pay rent.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e4_rd_prog_content
when concept=dreams.progress drive=content stage!=young
say I've decided I'm happy as I am. | Gave it up. Didn't miss it. | I sit by the fire and think about it. That's near enough.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=content 2m

rule e4_rd_prog_ambitious
when concept=dreams.progress drive=ambitious stage!=young
say Half there. The hard half. | Ahead of where I said I'd be. | I've a new one now. Bigger.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=good 2m

rule e4_rd_prog_young
when concept=dreams.progress stage=young
priority 3
say I'm bigger than last time! Look! | I practised all week. | Nearly! I can nearly reach the latch.
then other: dreams.reply
remember pair: e4d=pup 2m

## ================================================================ FAITH: asking and telling

rule e4_rf_ask_chapel
when concept=talk.faith
cooldown 1d
say Were you at chapel on Restday? | Do you go to chapel much? | Do you pray, #address#? Honestly? | Do you keep your prayers, these days?
then other: faith.answer

rule e4_rf_ask_belief
when concept=talk.faith self.stage!=young
cooldown 1d
say Do you believe it all? The Bright One and that? | What do you think happens to us, after? | Do you think the Bright One's listening? Really?
then other: faith.answer
remember pair: e4q=belief 2m

rule e4_rf_ask_close
when concept=talk.faith pair.band=friends|family|spouses
cooldown 2d
say Do you ever pray, #pet#? When nobody's looking? | Do you still go to chapel? You never say. | Do you still say your prayers at night, #pet#?
then other: faith.answer

rule e4_rf_ask_restday
when concept=talk.faith here.day=rest here.time=dawn|day
cooldown 1d
say Chapel this morning? | Bell's going. You coming? | Are you keeping Restday, then?
then other: faith.answer

rule e4_rf_ask_priest
when concept=talk.faith self.job=priest pair.flock=a
cooldown 2d
say Will I see you on Restday, #address#? | Are you keeping your prayers, #address#? | You'll come Restday? I've a good sermon ready.
then other: faith.answer

rule e4_rf_ask_pup
when concept=talk.faith other.stage=young self.stage=adult|old
cooldown 2d
say Do you know your prayers, #address#? | What did you learn at chapel? | Do you know who the Bright One is?
then other: faith.answer

rule e4_rf_tell_omen
when concept=talk.faith
cooldown 1d
say A bird flew in the window this morning. Out again before I could shout. | Shoes on the table. My mother'd have had a fit. Bad luck, that. | Itchy nose all morning. Somebody's thinking of me. | Saw a white hare on the road. Turned round and went home.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=omen 2m

rule e4_rf_tell_sermon
when concept=talk.faith self.priest self.piety=ordinary
cooldown 2d
say #self.priest# preached for an hour on Restday. On patience. Mine ran out. | #self.priest# says we should all give more. I gave a yawn. | #self.priest# had us sing the long hymn again. All the verses.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=sermon 2m

rule e4_rf_tell_sermon_plain
when concept=talk.faith self.job!=priest
cooldown 2d
say The priest found a new hymn. Twelve verses. We sang them all. | Did you hear the singing on Restday? Like cats in a sack. | The priest lost his place twice on Restday. Nobody minded.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=sermon 2m

rule e4_rf_tell_moved
when concept=talk.faith self.job!=priest
cooldown 2d
say The priest said something on Restday I can't stop thinking about. | The sermon was on mending quarrels. I went and mended one. | Restday's sermon was about the hungry. I've given away two loaves since.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=moved 2m

rule e4_rf_tell_devout
when concept=talk.faith self.piety=devout self.stage!=young
cooldown 2d
say I said the dawn prayer on the step this morning. It sets the day right. | The Bright One answered me this week. I'm sure of it. | I've been lighting a candle every night. For everyone.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=keen 2m

rule e4_rf_tell_doubt
when concept=talk.faith self.piety=ordinary self.honesty=frank
cooldown 3d
say I'll be honest. I don't know if anyone's up there. | I prayed for my father every night. Didn't help. | I've not felt a thing at chapel since I was a pup. Not a thing.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=doubt 2m

rule e4_rf_tell_charm
when concept=talk.faith
cooldown 2d
say I've a stone with a hole in it. Look through it and you see true. | Never cut your claws on Restday. Bad luck all week. | I keep a sprig of rowan in my coat. Not saying it works. Not saying it doesn't.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=omen 2m

rule e4_rf_tell_moon
when concept=talk.faith here.time=dusk|night
cooldown 2d
say Clouds over the moon. My gran wouldn't travel on a night like this. | Moon's got a ring round it. Weather coming, or worse. | Never point at the moon. My gran slapped my paw for it once.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=omen 2m

rule e4_rf_tell_mourning
when concept=talk.faith self.mourning=kin|friend
priority 2
cooldown 1d
say I keep setting a place for them. Then I remember. | I said the prayers for them. The words felt too small. | I talk to them at night. Is that daft?
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=grief 2m

rule e4_rf_tell_poor
when concept=talk.faith self.wealth=poor|destitute self.stage!=young
cooldown 3d
say Chapel says give thanks. For what, this week? A turnip? | The chapel bread's what keeps me. I'll say that for it. | I pray for supper. Some nights he listens.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e4_rf_tell_rich
when concept=talk.faith self.wealth=rich self.stage=adult|old
cooldown 3d
say I've paid for the new bell rope. They'll ring me in, at least. | I keep the chapel kitchen in bread. Nobody thanks you for bread, you know. | Charity's a duty, Mother said. So I do it. Mostly.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=rich 2m

rule e4_rf_tell_north
when concept=talk.faith self.from=frosthollow
cooldown 3d
say Up home nobody goes down the shaft without a word to the Stone Fathers. I still say it. | Up home we hang a lamp at the shaft-head for the ones still down there. | My gran said the old powers were in the mountain long before any chapel.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=folk 2m

rule e4_rf_tell_fen
when concept=talk.faith self.from=mirebridge
cooldown 3d
say Back home we hang a reed knot over the door. Keeps the damp spirits out. | Back home you never call a name across the water after dark. | The old fen folk name every eel-trap. For luck, they say.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=folk 2m

rule e4_rf_tell_south
when concept=talk.faith self.from=southmeadow|larkfield
cooldown 3d
say At home the last cart in from the harvest gets a ribbon on the horse. For luck. | We bake a loaf from the first grain and leave it on the chapel step. | Back home the eldest walks the bounds at midsummer, tapping the stones.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=folk 2m

rule e4_rf_tell_lake
when concept=talk.faith self.from=coldwater
cooldown 3d
say Back home we never say a drowned wolf's name on the water. Never. | Fishers back home leave the first fish of the year on the shore. For the lake. | Back home they ring a bell for the drowned. Every spring.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=folk 2m

rule e4_rf_tell_woods
when concept=talk.faith self.from=oakhaven
cooldown 3d
say Back home you ask a tree's leave before you fell it. Out loud. | We plant an acorn for every pup born, back home. Mine's a big oak now. | Some glades in the Warmwood, you lower your voice. Nobody tells you to. You just do.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=folk 2m

rule e4_rf_tell_tide
when concept=talk.faith here.region=ridgemere
cooldown 3d
say The Chapel of the Tide was packed this morning. Half the wharf. | They've hung a new lamp in the Chapel of the Tide. For the boats. | I said a prayer at the Tide chapel for the fishing boats.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=rite 2m

rule e4_rf_tell_storm
when concept=talk.faith here.weather=storm
cooldown 1d
say Listen to that. Every shutter in town's praying. | Storm like this, the old folk say the Dark One's testing the doors. | I've hung the iron over the door. Laugh if you like.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=omen 2m

rule e4_rf_tell_festival
when concept=talk.faith world.festival=soon|today here.festival
cooldown 2d
say I'm sewing a new banner for the chapel, for #here.festival#. | I'll keep the vigil the night before #here.festival#. I always do. | #here.festival#'s a holy day, before it's a feast. Folk forget.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=rite 2m

## ================================================================ FAITH: answering (self answers whether they go, or pray)

rule e4_rf_ans_plain
when concept=faith.answer piety=ordinary stage=adult|old
say When I can. Most weeks. Some weeks. | I go. I don't always listen. | Now and then. When things are bad, mostly. | I pray. I don't always know who's listening.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=lax 2m

rule e4_rf_ans_plain2
when concept=faith.answer piety=ordinary stage=adult|old
say I was there. Back bench. Half asleep. | Mother made us go. I still go, out of habit. | I say the words. I hope they land. | Restdays, mostly. Midwinter, always.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=lax 2m

rule e4_rf_ans_devout
when concept=faith.answer piety=devout stage=adult|old
say Every Restday. Front bench. | Every morning and every night, and in between. | Never miss. It's the best hour of my week.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=keen 2m

rule e4_rf_ans_dry
when concept=faith.answer piety=ordinary humour=dry
say Twice a year, and I sit near the stove. | I pray. I just don't think he's in. | We've a standing arrangement. I don't ask, he doesn't tell.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=lax 2m

rule e4_rf_ans_frank
when concept=faith.answer piety=ordinary honesty=frank
say No. I can't say I do. Not since my mother. | Not much. I work Restdays, and I'd not mean it. | Hardly. I've not prayed since I was a pup.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=doubt 2m

rule e4_rf_ans_sly
when concept=faith.answer honesty=sly stage=adult|old
say Course I was. Back row. Very quiet. | Every week, without fail. Ask anyone. Not the priest. | Devoutly. In spirit.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=sly 2m

rule e4_rf_ans_priest
when concept=faith.answer job=priest
priority 3
say I'd hope so. I give the sermons. | Every hour of the day. It's rather the job. | Most days. The other days I pray for patience with the rest of you.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=priest 2m

rule e4_rf_ans_guard
when concept=faith.answer job=guard|soldier stage=adult|old
say When the shifts let me. The Bright One knows where I was. | I pray at the gate. Quietly. Nobody's asked me to stop. | The captain says a prayer at muster. That's mine done.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=lax 2m

rule e4_rf_ans_innkeeper
when concept=faith.answer job=innkeeper|brewer piety=ordinary
say I hear more confessions over the bar than the priest does. | I pray the barrels last. | I keep a candle in the window. That's my chapel.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=lax 2m

rule e4_rf_ans_working
when concept=faith.answer working=yes here.day=rest
priority 1
say I'm working, #address#. Somebody has to. | Can't. Not today. I'll say one here, over the work. | Chapel doesn't sweep floors.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=work 2m

rule e4_rf_ans_poor
when concept=faith.answer wealth=poor|destitute piety=ordinary
say For the bread after, if I'm honest. | I pray every night. For supper. | They don't look at you kindly in rags.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e4_rf_ans_rich
when concept=faith.answer wealth=rich stage=adult|old
say Every Restday. Mother would rise from the grave otherwise. | I give. Generously. I'm told that's believing. | Of course. One is seen to be there.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=rich 2m

rule e4_rf_ans_heights
when concept=faith.answer quarter=heights wealth=rich|comfortable
say At the Chapel of the Tide. Our window's the blue one. | Of course. Everyone who's anyone goes. | Front pew. Where else?
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=rich 2m

rule e4_rf_ans_sump
when concept=faith.answer quarter=sump wealth!=rich
say Down here we pray at the Soup Kitchen. It's warmer. | The big chapel's not for the likes of us. Not really. | I pray. Down here you'd be daft not to.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e4_rf_ans_young
when concept=faith.answer stage=young
priority 4
say I know the start of the prayer. Not the middle. | We learned the Bright One went up. Up where? | I fidgeted. Mother pinched me. | I know the Bright One's star. It's the steady one.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=pup 2m

rule e4_rf_ans_old
when concept=faith.answer stage=old
priority 1
say Seventy years of Restdays. I've a few questions saved for him. | I go. My knees complain all through it. | More than I used to. You do, when it's nearer.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=old 2m

rule e4_rf_ans_mourning
when concept=faith.answer mourning=kin|friend stage!=young
priority 3
say I sat by them at the end, and prayed. I don't know if it helped. | I've been every day this week. Lighting candles. | I can't go. I'll cry in front of everyone.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=grief 2m

rule e4_rf_ans_north
when concept=faith.answer from=frosthollow stage=adult|old
say Chapel, aye. And a crust for the Stone Fathers. Both, to be safe. | Up home we keep the old ways and the chapel's. | The mountain's older than any chapel. I mind both.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=folk 2m

rule e4_rf_ans_fen
when concept=faith.answer from=mirebridge stage=adult|old
say Chapel, and the Fen Mother's words before I sleep. | Fen folk believe in everything. Safer. | I go. And I never follow the lights. That's my faith.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=folk 2m

rule e4_rf_ans_south
when concept=faith.answer from=southmeadow|larkfield stage=adult|old
say Harvest thanks, Restdays, all of it. And the corn wolf, quietly. | Every Restday. Then the orchard. | We bless the flocks at lambing. That's my chapel.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=folk 2m

## ================================================================ FAITH: answering what they believe (after e4_rf_ask_belief)

rule e4_rf_bel_plain
when concept=faith.answer pair.mem.e4q=belief
priority 3
say Most days. Ask me on a bad one. | I believe in something. Ask me what on a better day. | I'd like to. That's not nothing. | I think we go somewhere. I'd like it to be warm.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=lax 2m

rule e4_rf_bel_devout
when concept=faith.answer pair.mem.e4q=belief piety=devout
priority 3
say With all my heart. He's never let me down. | The Bright One went up so we'd have somewhere to follow. I believe that. | I do. I'd be lost without it.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=keen 2m

rule e4_rf_bel_frank
when concept=faith.answer pair.mem.e4q=belief piety=ordinary honesty=frank
priority 3
say Not since we buried my brother. | I don't know. Nobody does, if they're honest. | We go in the ground. The rest is singing.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=doubt 2m

rule e4_rf_bel_dry
when concept=faith.answer pair.mem.e4q=belief humour=dry piety=ordinary
priority 3
say I believe in the Bright One. I just don't think he believes in me. | After? Somebody else gets my chair. | He's listening. He's just not answering.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=lax 2m

rule e4_rf_bel_old
when concept=faith.answer pair.mem.e4q=belief stage=old
priority 4
say More every winter. | I'll find out soon enough, won't I. | I've buried enough to hope there's somewhere they went.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=old 2m

rule e4_rf_bel_priest
when concept=faith.answer pair.mem.e4q=belief job=priest
priority 5
say I believe. Some days it's hard work. Most days it's joy. | I'd not be wearing this if I didn't. | Every word. And I still have questions. He doesn't mind them.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=priest 2m

rule e4_rf_bel_mourning
when concept=faith.answer pair.mem.e4q=belief mourning=kin|friend
priority 5
say I have to. Or they're just gone. | This week? I don't know what I believe. | I'd like to think they're warm. I'd like that a lot.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=grief 2m

rule e4_rf_bel_young
when concept=faith.answer pair.mem.e4q=belief stage=young
priority 6
say Course! The Bright One's up there. Mother says. | He must be real. There's a chapel for him. | I think he watches. Even under the bed.
then other: faith.reply
remember pair: e4k=pup 2m

## ================================================================ FAITH: replying (self heard the answer, omen or belief)

rule e4_rf_rep_fallback
when concept=faith.reply
say Fair enough. | Each to their own. | Well. There it is.

# --- keen: the devout, at chapel and at prayer
rule e4_rf_rep_keen
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=keen
priority 1
say Good for you. | I wish I had your faith. | That's a comfort, that. | Bless you for it.

rule e4_rf_rep_keen_devout
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=keen piety=devout
priority 1
say The Bright One sees you. Remember that. | Come Restday. Sit by me. | Then we'll pray together, you and me.

rule e4_rf_rep_keen_frank
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=keen piety=ordinary honesty=frank
priority 1
say Good for you. I've forgotten how, myself. | I can't. But I'm glad somebody does. | Rather you than me.

rule e4_rf_rep_keen_priest
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=keen job=priest
priority 2
say Come and help with the candles, then. | The front bench thanks you. So do I. | I see you there. It helps, you know.

# --- lax: goes now and then, out of habit
rule e4_rf_rep_lax
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=lax
priority 1
say Fair enough. | Each to their own. | I'm much the same. | Well. There it is. | Can't hurt.

rule e4_rf_rep_lax_devout
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=lax piety=devout
priority 1
say I'll pray for you. No, I will. | Come and sit by me Restday. Nobody'll mind. | He hears you even from the back bench.

rule e4_rf_rep_lax_priest
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=lax job=priest
priority 2
say Come Restday. I'll save you a bench. | The Bright One hears more than you'd think. | My door's open. Any hour.

rule e4_rf_rep_lax_dry
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=lax humour=dry
priority 1
say The Bright One's got a lot to answer for. | I'll put in a word. Small one. | Same. I go for the company.

rule e4_rf_rep_lax_merry
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=lax humour=merry
priority 1
say Ha! Say one for me while you're at it. | Bless you. And your knees. | We'll sit at the back together and behave terribly.

# --- doubt: frank disbelief
rule e4_rf_rep_doubt
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=doubt
priority 1
say Fair. Nobody knows. | Keep that from the priest. | Hm. I go anyway. Just in case. | Honest, at least.

rule e4_rf_rep_doubt_devout
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=doubt piety=devout
priority 1
say Then I'll pray enough for both of us. | He believes in you, even if you don't. | It'll come back to you. It does.

rule e4_rf_rep_doubt_priest
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=doubt job=priest
priority 2
say Doubt's a prayer too, the way I see it. | Come and argue with me. I like it. | Then come and ask me why. I'll answer what I can.

rule e4_rf_rep_doubt_frank
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=doubt honesty=frank piety=ordinary
priority 1
say No. Nor me, if I'm honest. | Same. I'll believe it when he pays my rent. | Nor me. I still say grace, mind.

# --- sly: a plain fib
rule e4_rf_rep_sly
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=sly
priority 1
say Course you were. | I'm sure the Bright One noticed. | Mm. And I'm the High Priest. | Very quiet. I'll say.

rule e4_rf_rep_sly_priest
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=sly job=priest
priority 2
say I looked for you. Twice. | The Bright One sees the back row too. | And the rest of you was where?

rule e4_rf_rep_sly_sly
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=sly honesty=sly
priority 1
say Ha! Same bench as me, then. | I sat right by you. Didn't see you. Funny. | Saving the Bright One the trouble, eh?

# --- working on Restday
rule e4_rf_rep_work
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=work
priority 1
say Somebody has to. | He'll understand. | Say one on the job, then. | Next Restday, then.

rule e4_rf_rep_work_devout
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=work piety=devout
priority 1
say He sees it. Work's a kind of prayer. | I'll light a candle for you, then. | Say the short prayer. He knows you're busy.

rule e4_rf_rep_work_priest
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=work job=priest
priority 2
say Work well, then. That's a prayer of its own. | Then come at dusk. I'll be there. | The order needs its paws, Restday or not.

# --- omens, charms and old sayings
rule e4_rf_rep_omen
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=omen
priority 1
say Can't hurt to be careful. | I've heard that. | My gran said the same. | Strange, the things we hold to.

rule e4_rf_rep_omen_devout
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=omen piety=devout
priority 1
say Pray, and leave the rest to him. | Luck's the Dark One's coin. Pray instead. | I'll say a word for you. That's better than salt.

rule e4_rf_rep_omen_frank
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=omen honesty=frank piety=ordinary
priority 1
say It's just a thing that happened, #address#. | Superstition. Lovely, but superstition. | And if nothing comes of it?

rule e4_rf_rep_omen_priest
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=omen job=priest
priority 2
say Birds and salt and moons. Don't build a heresy out of them. | Superstition. But say a prayer anyway. Just in case. | There's no luck. There's the order, and our place in it.

rule e4_rf_rep_omen_old
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=omen stage=old
priority 1
say We all did that, in my day. | My mother said the same. Her mother too. | Mind it. The old sayings stick for a reason.

rule e4_rf_rep_omen_young
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=omen stage=young
priority 2
say Is that true? Really true? | That's scary. | Can I do it too?

rule e4_rf_rep_omen_north
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=omen from=frosthollow
priority 1
say Up home we'd leave a crust for that. | Lamp lit, crust left. Can't go wrong. | Up home they'd knock on stone, not wood.

rule e4_rf_rep_omen_fen
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=omen from=mirebridge
priority 1
say Fen folk'd say the same. | Put out milk. Can't hurt. | My gran would've hung a reed knot for that.

# --- the sermon, the priest, the singing
rule e4_rf_rep_sermon
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=sermon
priority 1
say I dozed. Don't tell. | Couldn't hear a thing past the pillar. | Sermons. Long, or longer. | Every week the same.

rule e4_rf_rep_sermon_devout
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=sermon piety=devout
priority 1
say Then sit nearer the front. You'll hear it better. | You should have listened. It was meant for you. | Hush. Not about chapel.

rule e4_rf_rep_sermon_priest
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=sermon job=priest
priority 2
say I'll pass that on. Kindly. | I give them too, you know. They're longer from the front. | Sermons are for the ones who don't want them.

rule e4_rf_rep_sermon_dry
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=sermon humour=dry
priority 1
say There are forty beams. I've counted. | Every sermon's the same one, turned inside out. | I give it a good nap, myself.

# --- a sermon that stuck
rule e4_rf_rep_moved
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=moved
priority 1
say Good. That's what they're for. | Some of them land. Not often, but some. | It stuck with me too. | Then it was worth the hard bench.

rule e4_rf_rep_moved_devout
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=moved piety=devout
priority 1
say It was meant for you. That's why. | The Bright One speaks through them, now and then. | Hold onto it. Say it over at night.

rule e4_rf_rep_moved_priest
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=moved job=priest
priority 2
say Then it did its work. Come and talk about it. | That's the best thing anyone's said to me all week. | Sit with it. Come and see me if it troubles you.

rule e4_rf_rep_moved_dry
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=moved humour=dry
priority 1
say Lucky. Mine slid right off. | Don't tell the priest. He'll do another. | First time for everything.

# --- the old ways of each region
rule e4_rf_rep_folk
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=folk
priority 1
say My gran did something like that. | Can't hurt. | Old ways. They hang on. | I've heard of that. Never seen it done.

rule e4_rf_rep_folk_priest
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=folk job=priest
priority 2
say I didn't hear that. I'm sure I didn't. | Old ways. Keep them if you must, but come to chapel as well. | The Bright One set the order. The rest is old wives, bless them.

rule e4_rf_rep_folk_devout
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=folk piety=devout
priority 1
say The Bright One's enough for me. But I'd not laugh at it. | Mind it doesn't take his place. | Pray as well, and you've both covered.

rule e4_rf_rep_folk_same
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=folk pair.same_from=yes
priority 2
say We did that too. Still do. | Course you do. We all do, back home. | My mother's the same. To the day.

# --- the rich at chapel
rule e4_rf_rep_rich
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=rich
priority 1
say Generous. | Somebody has to keep the roof on. | Very good of you. | The chapel's lucky in you.

rule e4_rf_rep_rich_poor
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=rich wealth=poor|destitute
priority 1
say Easy giving from a full purse. | Some of us are in the queue it feeds. | Must be nice, sitting down.

rule e4_rf_rep_rich_dry
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=rich humour=dry
priority 1
say And the Bright One sends his thanks, I'm sure. | He'll want twice as much next year. | They'll carve your name on something. They always do.

# --- the chapel's days: the Tide chapel, festivals
rule e4_rf_rep_rite
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=rite
priority 1
say I'll be there. | Best bit of the year. | Every year. Never tire of it. | I'll light one too.

rule e4_rf_rep_rite_young
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=rite stage=young
priority 2
say Can I carry a candle? | Can I come? Please? | Is it the one with the singing?

rule e4_rf_rep_rite_sailor
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=rite job=sailor|fisher
priority 1
say I like knowing somebody's praying, out there. | Light one for me next time. | Bless whoever lights them.

# --- a pup's answer
rule e4_rf_rep_pup
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=pup
priority 1
say That's a good start. | Good pup. Keep at it. | You'll have it all by heart soon. | Ha. Bless you.

rule e4_rf_rep_pup_pup
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=pup stage=young
priority 2
say Me too! | I know the middle! | Mother pinches me as well.

# --- the old
rule e4_rf_rep_old
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=old
priority 1
say You've earned that. | That's honest. | Not for a long while yet, I hope. | You'll outlast the lot of us.

rule e4_rf_rep_old_young
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=old stage=young
priority 2
say Will you tell me what he says? | Is it scary, being old? | Do your knees talk too?

# --- a priest's own answer
rule e4_rf_rep_priest
when concept=faith.reply pair.mem.e4k=priest
priority 1
say Fair. You'd know. | Ha. I suppose you would. | Rather you than me. | I envy you that.
